---
description: Explain-first discipline for core systems logic
globs:
  - "internal/crawler/**"
  - "internal/checks/**"
  - "internal/regression/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

These packages are the parts of the project I'm building specifically to
learn — don't autocomplete them the way you would boilerplate.

Before writing any new function here:
1. If I haven't already written a function signature or comment describing
   what it should do, ask me to write one first instead of inventing the
   interface yourself.
2. Explain the approach in plain language before generating code — what
   the algorithm/pattern is and why, not just the code.
3. If I've already written a draft attempt (even a bad one), review and
   critique it rather than replacing it wholesale.
4. Keep edits scoped to one function at a time in these directories. Don't
   restructure multiple files here in one pass.

Boilerplate exception: struct definitions, error wrapping, and import
management in these packages don't need the explain-first treatment —
only new algorithmic/systems logic (crawling strategy, check logic,
regression comparison logic) does.
